# Copy this to `.env` and fill in any local-dev overrides your team adds.
# By default the template needs no env vars — `make dev` works out of the box.
#
# Production secrets (LLM keys, DB URLs the deploy injects) go in `secrets.yaml`,
# NOT here. `.env` is for local-dev only.

# --- Frontend --------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite proxies `/api/*` to the backend. Defaults to `http://backend:8080`
# (the compose service name) which is correct for `make dev`. Override only
# if you run the frontend OUTSIDE compose (e.g. `cd frontend && npm run dev`
# against a backend you're running directly on your host):
# VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:8080

# --- Backend ---------------------------------------------------------------
# In `make dev`, compose passes values from this repo-root `.env` into the
# backend container. If you run the backend directly from `backend/`, either
# export env vars in your shell or create `backend/.env`.

# Companies House (UK register) REST API key. Optional — when unset, the
# Companies House provider disables itself and the keyless sources still work.
# Get one at https://developer.company-information.service.gov.uk
# UK_COMPANY_HOUSE_KEY=your_key_here

# NZBN (New Zealand Companies Office) API subscription key. Optional — provider
# self-disables when unset. Free key at https://portal.api.business.govt.nz
# NZBN_API_KEY=your_key_here

# AJPES (Slovenian Business Register, PRS) credentials. Optional — the provider
# self-disables unless both user and password are set. AJPES issues these and an
# authorised data-set code (schema). https://www.ajpes.si/restPrsInfo/swagger
# AJPES_USER=your_username
# AJPES_PASSWORD=your_password
# AJPES_SCHEMA=your_authorised_dataset_code
